{
  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on skewness, specifically preferring the lottery that is more right-skewed (i.e., has a higher probability assigned to unfavorable outcomes relative to favorable ones). To evaluate this, we need to assess the skewness of each lottery. Lottery A offers 500 Euros with 100% probability, which is a certain outcome and thus has no skewness (it is a degenerate distribution). Lottery B offers 1000 Euros with 50% probability and 0 Euros with 50% probability. Since the lower outcome (0 Euros) has a higher probability than the higher outcome (1000 Euros), Lottery B is right-skewed. Lottery A, being certain, is not skewed. Therefore, the decision reason would prefer Lottery B because it is more right-skewed than A. The information required to apply this reason is available in the problem.",
